# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. `.env*` is gitignored, so `.env.local` never
# reaches the repository — this file is the committed record of what needs to
# exist for a full build.
#
# `output: "export"` inlines every NEXT_PUBLIC_ value into the JavaScript bundle
# at build time. Changing one needs a rebuild and a redeploy, not just a dev
# server restart, and none of them can hold anything secret: they are all
# readable in devtools on the deployed site. Nothing here is a secret.


# ── Contact form ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Without these two the form silently degrades to a `mailto:` handoff, which
# loses the enquiry outright on a phone with no mail client configured.
#
# Web3Forms identifies the destination inbox by the access key in the request
# body, so both values are needed. The key is public by design; it can only
# cause mail to be sent to the configured inbox, never read from it.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CONTACT_ENDPOINT=https://api.web3forms.com/submit
NEXT_PUBLIC_CONTACT_ACCESS_KEY=


# ── Site origin ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Only needed for preview deploys on a different hostname. Left unset, the build
# uses the real domain (see SITE_URL in src/lib/site.ts), which is what
# production wants — a canonical tag pointing at a preview host is how the site
# ended up telling Google its pages lived on a domain that no longer resolved.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://hivecrest.tech


# ── Employee Management System ────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Both null until the EMS is reachable. See the notes on EMPLOYEE_LOGIN_URL and
# EMPLOYEE_LOGIN_ENDPOINT in src/lib/site.ts for what the endpoint must do.
# Must be https: a password over http is readable in transit.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_EMS_URL=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_EMS_LOGIN_ENDPOINT=
